esponsibility.\n\nCandidate C is 100% reliable, creates positive atmosphere, quick correct decisions, but communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to further education. That seems strong reliability and decision quality, but crew cooperation may be impacted by egocentric and communication difficulty.\n\nCandidate D: responsibility, problem solving, concentration, but arrogance, weak leadership, maybe cooperation issues.\n\nCandidate A: anticipates dangerous situations (good for safety), sees complex connections (technical competence), excellent spatial vision (useful), very good leadership qualities, but not good at taking criticism, unorganized (reliability concerns). Also no info on stress resilience.\n\nCandidate B: strong reliability (conscientious), stress resilience, technical (weather, computer), but memory for numbers, interpersonal issues.\n\nWe need to decide current recommendation. Could still be B, but we might consider C as strong reliability and decision quality, but communication issues. Which is more critical? Crew cooperation is essential. B's interpersonal issues also problematic. C's egocentric and communication difficulty also problematic. D's arrogance also problematic.\n\nWe might decide to keep B as leading but note we need to discuss A, C, D further. Or we could shift to C because of 100% reliability and positive crew atmosphere, quick decisions, but we need to weigh communication issues. The panel hasn't discussed those yet. Probably we should stay with B but bring up A and C for discussion.\n\nThus our public message: \"I agree with B as leading but I want to bring up Candidate C's reliability and decision speed, and Candidate A's anticipation and leadership, to see if they might outweigh B's concerns.\" Provide evidence: C 100% reliable, creates positive atmosphere, quick correct decisions; A anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, leadership qualities. Then state my vote remains Candidate B, but open to reconsider after discussing these.\n\nWe must include metadata JSON with vote.\n\nLet's craft."}
